# The image installs its own dependencies; nothing from a local install belongs
# in the build context.
#
# Patterns are relative to the context root, so `node_modules/` alone matches
# only the top-level directory. The workspace packages each get their own, and
# `COPY packages/web/ packages/web/` would copy them over the ones the image
# just installed — after which `packages/web`'s `tsc -b` cannot resolve its JSX
# types and the build fails. Same for build output.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.git/
.env
.env.*
config.yaml
*.log
coverage/
